---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../../styles/portfolio.css';
---

<Base
  title="Wënü Mäpü — Brand + Product Case Study · OCÍN"
  description="Wënü Mäpü case study by Nicolás Ortega / Ocín: founder-led brand, physical product, photography, e-commerce and digital experience."
  robots="noindex, nofollow"
  noNav={true}
  noFooter={true}
  noOverlays={true}
  noQuote={true}
  noThemes={true}
  noKai={true}
  noCart={true}
  noImmersive={true}
>
  <div class="pf">
    <header class="pf-nav">
      <div class="pf-shell pf-nav__inner">
        <a class="pf-wordmark" href="/portfolio">OCÍN <small>Portfolio</small></a>
        <nav class="pf-nav__links" aria-label="Portfolio">
          <a href="/portfolio">Work</a>
          <a href="/">Live Wënü</a>
          <a href="mailto:ocinkey8@gmail.com">Contact</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="pf-case-hero">
      <div class="pf-shell">
        <div class="pf-case-hero__grid" data-pf-reveal>
          <div>
            <p class="pf-kicker">Case 02 / Founder-led commercial system</p>
            <h1>Wënü Mäpü</h1>
          </div>
          <p class="pf-case-hero__lede">
            An independent body-jewelry brand built across physical product, visual identity,
            photography, e-commerce, storytelling and customer experience.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="pf-case-meta" data-pf-reveal>
          <div><span class="pf-meta">Role</span><strong>Founder / Creative Director</strong></div>
          <div><span class="pf-meta">Type</span><strong>Physical + digital brand</strong></div>
          <div><span class="pf-meta">Focus</span><strong>Product + commerce + identity</strong></div>
          <div><span class="pf-meta">Constraint</span><strong>Real customers + operations</strong></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="pf-feature" data-pf-reveal>
      <img src="/img/hero/hero-body-eclipse.webp" alt="Wënü Mäpü body jewelry campaign" />
    </div>

    <section class="pf-shell pf-case-block">
      <div data-pf-reveal><p class="pf-label">Challenge</p><h2>Build a world without making the product harder to understand.</h2></div>
      <div class="pf-case-block__body" data-pf-reveal>
        <p>
          Wënü Mäpü needed a strong point of view across material, body, culture and ritual while
          still functioning as a real product business. The challenge was not simply visual identity:
          customers still needed to understand what a piece was, how it was made or specified, what
          it cost and how to buy it.
        </p>
        <p>
          That tension taught me to separate narrative depth from commercial friction. The universe can
          be rich; the path to product information and purchase has to stay direct.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pf-shell pf-case-block">
      <div data-pf-reveal><p class="pf-label">My role</p><h2>Creative direction under real constraints.</h2></div>
      <div class="pf-case-block__body" data-pf-reveal>
        <p>
          As founder and creative director, I work across the whole system rather than one isolated deliverable.
          That includes identity, product curation, photography, merchandising, e-commerce, storytelling and
          day-to-day decisions around suppliers, customers and digital sales.
        </p>
        <ul class="pf-list">
          <li>Brand positioning + creative direction</li>
          <li>Product curation + presentation</li>
          <li>Macro product and editorial photography</li>
          <li>E-commerce structure + merchandising</li>
          <li>Web experience + information architecture</li>
          <li>Packaging and product-information concepts</li>
          <li>Supplier, customer, content and sales decisions</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pf-section">
      <div class="pf-shell">
        <div class="pf-section__head" data-pf-reveal>
          <p class="pf-label">Brand evidence</p>
          <div>
            <h2>Material first. Atmosphere second. Clarity always.</h2>
            <p class="pf-section__intro">
              The visual system is dark, editorial and material-led, but product detail and commerce
              remain legible. The goal is not “tribal decoration”; it is a contemporary brand system with
              disciplined cultural and material references.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="pf-media-grid">
          <figure data-pf-reveal><img src="/img/brand/meteorite-final.webp" alt="Wënü Mäpü meteorite material photography" loading="lazy" /></figure>
          <figure data-pf-reveal><img src="/img/categories/cat-piercing.webp" alt="Wënü Mäpü piercing product category" loading="lazy" /></figure>
          <figure data-pf-reveal><img src="/img/brand/shop-ritual-septum-hero.webp" alt="Wënü Mäpü ritual septum campaign" loading="lazy" /></figure>
          <figure data-pf-reveal><img src="/img/hero/hero-eclipse-1200w.webp" alt="Wënü Mäpü eclipse campaign visual" loading="lazy" /></figure>
          <figure data-pf-reveal><img src="/img/brand/artistry-workbench.webp" alt="Wënü Mäpü material and workbench imagery" loading="lazy" /></figure>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pf-shell pf-case-block">
      <div data-pf-reveal><p class="pf-label">System thinking</p><h2>The brand is more than the logo.</h2></div>
      <div class="pf-case-block__body" data-pf-reveal>
        <p>
          The system has to work across photography, product pages, categories, editorial content,
          packaging concepts and customer support. I use a shared grammar — typography, image treatment,
          hierarchy, tone and material emphasis — while allowing commerce pages to be more explicit than
          atmospheric editorial spaces.
        </p>
        <p>
          This is where Wënü Mäpü connects directly to my Creative Technologist practice: the problem is
          not producing more assets, but defining enough rules that different outputs remain coherent.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pf-shell pf-case-block">
      <div data-pf-reveal><p class="pf-label">Real-world constraints</p><h2>Every design decision eventually meets operations.</h2></div>
      <div class="pf-case-block__body" data-pf-reveal>
        <ul class="pf-list">
          <li>Physical inventory, variants and availability</li>
          <li>Material, sizing and compatibility information</li>
          <li>Supplier data and product provenance</li>
          <li>Photography production and asset consistency</li>
          <li>Checkout, shipping, returns and care information</li>
          <li>Customer questions and education</li>
          <li>Clear distinction between cultural narrative and verifiable product claims</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pf-shell pf-case-block">
      <div data-pf-reveal><p class="pf-label">Outcome</p><h2>A functioning brand, not a speculative mockup.</h2></div>
      <div class="pf-case-block__body" data-pf-reveal>
        <p>
          Wënü Mäpü exists as a founder-led brand spanning physical product, photography, e-commerce,
          identity, content and operational decision-making. I deliberately avoid presenting unverified
          business metrics in this case; the strongest evidence is the functioning system itself and the
          constraints it has had to survive.
        </p>
        <div class="pf-actions">
          <a class="pf-btn pf-btn--primary" href="/">Open live Wënü Mäpü</a>
          <a class="pf-btn" href="https://www.behance.net/wenumapu" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Behance</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="pf-shell pf-next">
      <a href="/portfolio/kodex">← KODEX-∞</a>
      <a href="/portfolio">Portfolio →</a>
    </div>

    <footer class="pf-shell pf-footer">
      <span class="pf-meta">Nicolás Ortega / Ocín</span>
      <span class="pf-meta">Creative Technologist</span>
    </footer>
  </div>

  <script>
    (() => {
      const items = document.querySelectorAll('[data-pf-reveal]');
      if (!('IntersectionObserver' in window)) {
        items.forEach((el) => el.classList.add('is-visible'));
        return;
      }
      const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
        for (const entry of entries) {
          if (entry.isIntersecting) {
            entry.target.classList.add('is-visible');
            observer.unobserve(entry.target);
          }
        }
      }, { threshold: 0.08, rootMargin: '0px 0px -48px 0px' });
      items.forEach((el) => observer.observe(el));
    })();
  </script>
</Base>
